{"reference":"1 Kings 6","book":"1 Kings","chapter":6,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"A Comparative Question","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"The temple’s architecture and craftsmanship can be compared with temples elsewhere in the Levant and wider ancient Near East. Such comparison, however, should not obscure this narrative’s distinctive emphases on the LORD’s name, covenant, prayer, and the fact that God cannot be contained.","verse_refs":["1 Kings 6:1-38"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_1_kings_006_259fa96ce17d7e4820a4a156"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}